d1: stub -> recursive carries note="recursive query" description="One question: find example.com for me."
d2: recursive -> cache checks note="checks first" description="A cached answer ends the lookup here, one round trip from the stub."
d3: recursive -> root carries note="where is .com?" description="Only on a cold cache. The .com referral is almost always cached."
d4: recursive -> tld carries note="where is example.com?"
d5: recursive -> auth carries note="what is example.com?"
d6: auth -> recursive produces note="A 93.184.216.34" description="The answer and its TTL."
d7: recursive -> tcp-fallback retries note="TC bit set" description="The answer did not fit in the UDP reply."
d8: tcp-fallback -> auth carries note="same query over TCP"
d9: recursive -> stub produces note="answer" description="The stub hands the address back to the browser."
